 is that your motivation  your attitude your passion they all talk  about this your confidence your whole  mindset towards language learning is the  overwhelming factor and if you have that  interest and that's obvious by listening  to these people that they all had this  passion as I do particularly my later  years here for learning languages and  the confidence and that they liked the  language again Richard goes into this  whole idea again of loving the language  at its armies from listening to the  others that they love learning these  languages so the attitude is absolutely  paramount the second thing is that you  have to put in a time if you listen to  them they have all put in a lot of time  there is no you know other than daniel  Tammet who has some unique artistic  ability to learn most people put in a  fair amount of time but again in order  to put in the time you have to like what  you're doing and so that's why you know  some of the specific techniques that  Luca uses or richer users or or some of  the others use Susannah and so forth I  wouldn't I don't like doing those things  and therefore those are not things that  I would do so in order for me to be able  to put in the time I've got to do the  things that I like to do in the sequence  that I like to do and this is another  thing that's some some of us I mean we  all like to talk but you know at what  point we all recognize the need to refer  to grammar in some way whether we're  specifically looking at grammar  explanations or whether we are studying  as Luca does the language he's learning  and comparing it to a language he knows  very well in order to  identify the structural differences and  how concepts are presented in the new  language whatever it is you have to have  some way that you're dealing with the  issue of of grammatical structure but we  can all do it our own way in a way that  we like so again to kind of repeat it  you got to have that attitude you got to  put in the time and then the third thing  is you've got to find some way of  helping your brain notice what's going  on hopefully a way that you like but  this then it gets back to the idea of  you know Lucas techniques both Luca and  Richard liked bilingual text I don't I  find them distracting but everyone is  you know they are very successful  polyglots linguist more successful than  I am I don't know whether on a per you  know unit of time input basis they are  but in terms of the net result they  certainly are more proficient than I am  in most languages so you know their  system works for them I don't like doing  it so it wouldn't work for me so but I  recognize that I have to do things to  help me notice for example one thing  I've started doing now in my Russian  when I read away from the computer since  I now know you know I very few words if  I'm reading through coast or I'm reading  out a book by rosinski advances key on  the history I think the biography of  Alexander the second I go through there  and I have decided to give each case in  Russian a number nominative is one  accusative his two genitive is three  dative is for instrumental is five and  the prepositional case is six so I write  in a little number 136 right above the  nouns and adjectives and if it's plural  I write it twice what does it do it  forces me to think about the structure  it forces me to get a grasp not only of  that specific adjective and noun but of  the overall way these things work I  understand it in principle I have for  many years but I have trouble nailing  them down when I'm speaking I regularly  make mistakes with my cases so I'm now  forcing myself to pay attention  so this is again a way to increase our  ability to notice Luca has techniques  with regard to working on your  pronunciation obviously you have to  notice you have to hear the  pronunciation otherwise you can't  imitate it so again in listening to  these I recommend that you listen to  them I've enjoyed them and they have  only confirmed me in my belief that the  big three attitude time on task and  improving your ability to notice are the  keys and that the way we do that can  vary from individual to individual and  yeah there we are and the polyglots  linguists are all over the world  everywhere I go I meet them and it's not  something that we are born with and some  kind of a genetic gift it's it's very  much something that we're all capable of  doing so thank you for listening and if  you have any specific subjects that you  would like me to raise with Richard sim  card when we speak on Sunday please let  me know bye for now
 

